From b1af3a261c03050585e21f48fe449323015c713f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: martino-dot <martin@blurrmc.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:10:58 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Support tubes that are straight, then curved, then
 straight

A tube can now be defined by the length before the curve, the curve
length, and the length after the curve (Tube.from_lengths, or the new
optional length_before_curve / curve_length fields on Tube).

- Tube: curve placement, validation, curvature_at(), curve_interval,
  has_uniform_curvature. Tubes built the old way are unchanged (curved
  over their whole length).
- Segment: now carries the curvature of each active tube, since a tube
  can be present but straight within a segment.
- backbone_segments: also splits at the start and end of each tube's
  curve, merges coincident boundaries (1e-12 m), and records
  per-segment curvatures.
- torsion_v2 / curvature: use the per-segment curvature instead of
  Tube.precurvature. The torsion coupling formula itself is untouched.
- V1 solve_forward_kinematics raises NotImplementedError for these
  tubes instead of silently treating them as fully curved.
- ROS simulator: robot defined by an editable TUBE_CONFIG table using
  the three lengths (defaults reproduce the previous robot).
- Example, docs, and 36 new tests.

Uniformly curved robots give bit-identical results to before.
